        "lead_summary": "The barbell finally did what barbells do: it balanced. META +13.0% \u2014 a third of the fund's September gain arriving in five sessions on the Muse agent's momentum and Friday's AI tape \u2014 carried XLC to a +1.9% week and a 50-day reclaim, even while the distribution half completed its collapse: CHTR -11.9% for a THIRD straight week near -12%, CMCSA and TMUS at fresh 52-week-low closes, VZ's yield cushion thinning to 70bp against a 5.18% ten-year. The fund closed $112.96, two dollars under the 200-day, with the wildest internal divergence of any sector board: one engine at 52-week highs, the other at 52-week lows, in the same ETF. The October 2 Google final judgment and the late-October broadband prints will decide which half is the fund.",
